{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/97240-necessity-for-epics-and-successes","id":97240,"title":"Necessity for epics and successes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-23T20:23:09-07:00","id":97240,"title":"Necessity for epics and successes","content":"When it comes to epic strength, it is pretty easy to understand what you get for your epic successes rating. Generally you are trying to hurt/break something or lift something. In the latter there is the chart when spells out exactly what you can lift. But what about the other attributes? What kind of feats would separate two separate actions, one requiring 10 successes and the other requiring 20. What about appearance? Who could you woo with no less than 30 successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T12:05:00-07:00","id":97648,"title":"","content":"I'm certain that there's a &quot;Your Mum&quot; joke in there somewhere.<br /> <br /> I can say that this has never really come up (requiring a hard &amp; fast list) for the other physical attributes or the Mentals.<br /> As for the Socials, it's rather easy enough to say that you need &quot;equal or better&quot; Epics to deal with other legendary characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T12:58:29-07:00","id":97683,"title":"","content":"For anything physical or mental: Whatever arbitrary number the storyteller decides is appropriate, or someone else's contested roll.<br /> For anything social: Whatever the mental defense stat of your opponent is, or someone else's contested roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T18:07:45-07:00","id":97938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/97240-necessity-for-epics-and-successes?p=97683#post97683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For anything physical or mental: Whatever arbitrary number the storyteller decides is appropriate, or someone else's contested roll.<br /> For anything social: Whatever the mental defense stat of your opponent is, or someone else's contested roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I usually do the arbitrary thing. But it feels so, arbitrary. I mean what kind of successes would one require to, for example, find a single hair left on a shag carpet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T18:15:57-07:00","id":97944,"title":"","content":"What is the difficulty to see a single hair? Then start adding modifiers.<br /> <br /> Basic point being, identify the difficulty of a task in its simplest form, which is probably within human limits, and apply modifiers for what makes it difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","user":"Hark","date":". 03-24-2014, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T21:12:30-07:00","id":98058,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I've had an idea on how to visualize successes and difficulties. <br /> <br /> 5 is the mortal cap on Attributes, Abilities, and equipment bonuses. 2 is the mortal average for Attributes, and the general mortal probably has at least one dot of most, if not all, Abilities, and most tools would probably only give one additional. So, let's say you're going to research something, an Intelligence + Academics roll. A typical mortal is going to have 3-4 dice for their pool, which averages to 2 successes. The worlds smartest mortal, who has trained extensively in the subject, inside a library with the world's most comprehensive resources on the topic, is going to have a pool of 15 dice, which will translate to an average of 7 successes. And, of course, the insanely unlikely theoretical maximum that anyone could get on a roll is to receive all tens, which means that the pool of 15 dice has a maximum of 30 successes, and that is a freak occurrence that would be less likely than random lightning bolts striking the entire crew of Serenity at the same time. <br /> <br /> So, to try and put this on a scale... <br /> <br /> 5 successes - Challenging for the average mortal. Easy for exceptional mortals (Acing a calculus exam, performing an opera)<br /> 10 successes - Challenging, but doable for exceptional mortals (Selling the Eiffel Tower, trailing a guy in Grand Central Station at rush hour)<br /> 15 successes - Extremely challenging for exceptional mortals (Walking into a den of starving lions and surviving, finding a needle in a haystack)<br /> 20 successes - If possible at all, it requires a huge amount of time and effort, even by exceptional mortals (Finding one specific needle in a stack of needles, convincing Kim Jong Un to step down and dismantle North Korea's nuclear program)<br /> 30 successes - Practically impossible, anyone who did it would be immortalized (Convincing someone they were actually a yellow-footed rock wallaby, turn lead into gold)<br /> Above 30 - Completely impossible for mortals <br /> <br /> And, keep in mind, by the time you hit god and are dealing with 30+ successes, you're working alongside and against beings who are also throwing around those successes on average. If someone has Epic Appearance 10, you'll need Epic Charisma or Manipulation 10 to seduce them if they're not interested. If someone has Epic Manipulation 10, you'll need Epic Perception or Intelligence 10 to divine their true motivations and plans if they're trying to hide them. If someone has Epic Perception 10, you'll need Epic Wits or Dexterity 10 to successfully hide from them. It's an arms race, essentially","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T04:20:51-07:00","id":98257,"title":"","content":"I've always thought Strength being a special case, having charts and tables and things, was strange. It's tough to define the other attributes by anything but the arbitrary difficulty of tasks. Gotham By Night has developed a Perception table which seems to work well for them, but I haven't tried it myself.<br /> <br /> I guess you could say that Stamina has a sort of &quot;hidden&quot; effect chart, when you start comparing autosuccesses to the stats of poisons and environmental effects, but that's not too satisfying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1160-luminous-crayon","name":"Luminous Crayon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T05:43:25-07:00","id":98291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucidFeverDream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/97240-necessity-for-epics-and-successes?p=97938#post97938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I usually do the arbitrary thing. But it feels so, arbitrary. I mean what kind of successes would one require to, for example, find a single hair left on a shag carpet.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>It's always arbitrary.</b> The strength chart we are provided with now is arbitrary. Someone first decides the value of a success, then extrapolates that into a usable chart. But the initial decision about the value of a success is always arbitrary.<br /> <br /> GriffinGuy has provided a fairly decent guideline for mortal capability. My personal baseline tends to be about 20 successes for introductory Demigod, 40 successes for introductory God, and 80 successes for Legend 12 Gods. It is totally possible to score more successes than this, but this is about the minimum you should be throwing at something you claim to be good at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T05:45:08-07:00","id":99941,"title":"","content":"&quot;Completely arbitrary&quot; is basically it. The question did come up a lot in my games - it's very easy to tell what a Scion can do with epic physicals, because being fast, strong, and tough is reasonably well-defined and understood by basically anyone, and things you could use your epic physicals on are statted to include the attributes that resist your efforts. What isn't understood by basically anyone are question like: How much can superhuman beauty actually do to characters you care about? Can you wrap a stereotypical Scion of Ares who's threatening to hurt the band around your little finger with Epic Appearance of 2? What about 3? Can you shout &quot;Hey! An Airplane!&quot; and get him to look up with Epic Manipulation of 2? But what if he also has a high Wits score? We know you can spend Willpower to resist mental influence from the powers of knacks and purviews, but there is no actual system for social interaction outside of that. If social abilities are one third of the powers you could theoretically have, that is really sad.<br /> It's even less clear for epic mental ability and the things you'd actually want a Scion of Dian Cecht to do - nobody in the world can tell you exactly how hard it is to invent an AIDS vaccine or heal a paraplegic without boons, and your storyteller probably isn't a virologist or neurologist who could give a reasonable estimate. Nobody in the world can tell you how hard it is to hack the global surveillance program of an intelligence agency of your choice, and again, your ST is likely not a hacker who can estimate it.<br /> <br /> Scion basically does not give you any system besides &quot;use your own best judgement&quot; to understand what an Intelligence+Medicine dicepool of thirty actually means. It does nowhere tell you what mysteries your epically intelligent and perceptive occult detective can figure out as easily as the team's physical powerhouse can smash through concrete. Which means your power to easily resolve mystery ploys rests entirely on the assumption that the ST will honour your investment and declare success or failure on a fair, yet arbitrary basis - and you would not need to buy Scion if you're going to resort to arbitrary declarations and hope for fairness anyway.<br /> <br /> The game could give you an idea of what an Appearance+Presence dicepool of thirty actually meant because social rolls are usually opposed in some fashion. But there is no standard attribute for resisting social moves that you could compare to typical NPC stats, so again, nobody can give you an official answer what that is supposed to mean. Griffin's homemade system above is what you will have to resort to, because the book does not give a satisfactory answer. It's a reasonable first assumption, and it's still just a systematic approach to &quot;your ST makes arbitrary decisions based on NPC stats and gut feelings about the actual possibility/impossibility of the task&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2601-nachtigallerator","name":"Nachtigallerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}